/* The reason iOS shows when Lunaway first asks for the position. Each key
   of Info.plist ending in UsageDescription has a line here and in
   fr.lproj/InfoPlist.strings. */
"NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription" = "Lunaway shows your position on the map, sorts the places around you and guides you along a route you start. To compute a route, your position goes to Lunaway's server, which keeps nothing of it; to look for fuel along the route, an approximate position. It also goes there when you add a place where you stand.";
